{"id":"88de38a6ccdc5e769469423dfe0ae6ed26a850cd","axis":"silent","repo":"dotnet/runtime","sha":"88de38a6ccdc5e769469423dfe0ae6ed26a850cd","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/jit-format.yml","lines":["@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ jobs:","         os:","           - name: linux","             image: ubuntu-latest","-            container: mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net11.0-cross-amd64","+            container: mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net12.0-cross-amd64","             extension: '.sh'","             cross: '--cross'","             rootfs: '/crossrootfs/x64'"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Directory.Build.props","lines":["@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@","     <NetFrameworkToolCurrent Condition=\"'$(DotNetBuildSourceOnly)' == 'true'\" />","     <NetFrameworkCurrent Condition=\"'$(DotNetBuildSourceOnly)' == 'true'\" />"," ","-    <ApiCompatNetCoreAppBaselineVersion>11.0.0-rc.1.26425.128</ApiCompatNetCoreAppBaselineVersion>","+    <ApiCompatNetCoreAppBaselineVersion>11.0.0-rc.3.26522.148</ApiCompatNetCoreAppBaselineVersion>","     <ApiCompatNetCoreAppBaselineTFM>net11.0</ApiCompatNetCoreAppBaselineTFM>","   </PropertyGroup>"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/project/dogfooding.md","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@"," # Dogfooding daily builds of .NET"," "," This document provides the steps necessary to consume a latest development build of .NET runtime and SDK.","-Example below is for 11.0.","+Example below is for 12.0."," "," ## Obtaining daily builds of NuGet packages"," ","@@ -14,14 +14,14 @@ dotnet new nugetconfig"," "," Next, add the package source to NuGet.Config with the [dotnet nuget add source](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-nuget-add-source) command:"," ```","-dotnet nuget add source -n dotnet11 https://dnceng.pkgs.visualstudio.com/public/_packaging/dotnet11/nuget/v3/index.json","+dotnet nuget add source -n dotnet12 https://dnceng.pkgs.visualstudio.com/public/_packaging/dotnet12/nuget/v3/index.json"," ```"," "," Then, you will be able to add the latest prerelease version of the desired package to your project."," ","-**Example:** To add version 11.0-alpha.1.24556.8 of the System.Data.OleDb package, use the [dotnet add package](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-add-package) command:","+**Example:** To add version 12.0.0-alpha.1.26528.120 of the System.Data.OleDb package, use the [dotnet add package](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-add-package) command:"," ```","-dotnet add package System.Data.OleDb -v 11.0-alpha.1.24556.8","+dotnet add package System.Data.OleDb -v 12.0.0-alpha.1.26528.120"," ```"," "," To use daily builds of the entire runtime, follow the steps given in the rest of this document instead.","@@ -31,12 +31,12 @@ To use daily builds of the entire runtime, follow the steps given in the rest of"," If you're using private Azure DevOps feeds for your projects, you might need to add the preview feed through the Azure-specific feed URI format, which is `azure-feed://organization/optionalProject/feed@view`. In this case, you can add the .NET development package feed as follows:"," "," ```","-azure-feed://dnceng/public/dotnet11@Local","+azure-feed://dnceng/public/dotnet12@Local"," ```"," "," ## Install prerequisites"," ","-1. Acquire the latest development .NET SDK by downloading and extracting a zip/tarball or using an installer from the [latest builds table in dotnet/sdk](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk#installing-the-sdk) (for example, https://aka.ms/dotnet/11.0/daily/dotnet-sdk-win-x64.zip).","+1. Acquire the latest development .NET SDK by downloading and extracting a zip/tarball or using an installer from the [latest builds table in dotnet/sdk](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk#installing-the-sdk) (for example, https://aka.ms/dotnet/12.0/daily/dotnet-sdk-win-x64.zip)."," "," 2. If you are using a local copy of the dotnet CLI, take care that when you type `dotnet` you do not inadvertently pick up a different copy that you may have in your path. On Windows, for example, if you use a Command Prompt, a global copy may be in the path, so use the fully qualified path to your local `dotnet` (e.g. `C:\\dotnet\\dotnet.exe`). If you receive an error \"error NETSDK1045:  The current .NET SDK does not support targeting .NET 12.0.\" then you may be executing an older `dotnet`."," ","@@ -44,29 +44,29 @@ After setting up dotnet you can verify you are using the current preview version"," ```"," >dotnet --info"," .NET SDK:","- Version:   11.0.100-alpha.1.24556.7","- Commit:    fc127ac5a4","+ Version:   12.0.100-alpha.1.26528.120","+ Commit:    bc397b207b"," "," Runtime Environment:","  OS Name:     Windows","  OS Version:  10.0.22616","  OS Platform: Windows","  RID:         win-x64","- Base Path:   C:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\sdk\\11.0.100-alpha.1.24556.7\\","+ Base Path:   C:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\sdk\\12.0.100-alpha.1.26528.120\\"," "," global.json file:","   Not found"," "," Host:","-  Version:      12.0.0-alpha.1.24556.3","+  Version:      12.0.0-alpha.1.26528.120","   Architecture: x64","-  Commit:       47d9c43ab1","+  Commit:       bc397b207b"," "," .NET SDKs installed:","-  11.0.100-alpha.1.24556.7 [C:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\sdk]","+  12.0.100-alpha.1.26528.120 [C:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\sdk]"," "," .NET runtimes installed:","-  Microsoft.NETCore.App 12.0.0-alpha.1.24556.7 [C:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\shared\\Microsoft.NETCore.App]","+  Microsoft.NETCore.App 12.0.0-alpha.1.26528.120 [C:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\shared\\Microsoft.NETCore.App]"," "," Download .NET:","   https://aka.ms/dotnet-download","@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@ Learn about .NET Runtimes and SDKs:"," 3. Our daily builds are uploaded to development feed, not NuGet - so ensure the development feed is in your nuget configuration in case you need other packages that aren't included in the download. For example, on Windows you could edit `%userprofile%\\appdata\\roaming\\nuget\\nuget.config` or on Linux edit `~/.nuget/NuGet/NuGet.Config` to add these lines:"," ```xml"," <packageSources>","-    <add key=\"dotnet11\" value=\"https://dnceng.pkgs.visualstudio.com/public/_packaging/dotnet11/nuget/v3/index.json\" />","+    <add key=\"dotnet12\" value=\"https://dnceng.pkgs.visualstudio.com/public/_packaging/dotnet12/nuget/v3/index.json\" />","     ..."," </packageSources>"," ```"],"additions":14,"deletions":14,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/workflow/building/coreclr/cross-building.md","lines":["@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@ docker run --rm \\","   -v <RUNTIME_REPO_PATH>:/runtime \\","   -w /runtime \\","   -e ROOTFS_DIR=/crossrootfs/arm64 \\","-  mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net11.0-cross-arm64 \\","+  mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net12.0-cross-arm64 \\","   ./build.sh --subset clr --cross --arch arm64"," ```"," ","@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ docker run --rm \\","   -v <RUNTIME_REPO_PATH>:/runtime \\","   -w /runtime \\","   -e ROOTFS_DIR=/crossrootfs/x64 \\","-  mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net11.0-cross-freebsd-14-amd64 \\","+  mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net12.0-cross-freebsd-14-amd64 \\","   ./build.sh --subset clr --cross --os freebsd"," ```"," ","@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ docker run --rm -it \\","   -v $(pwd):/runtime \\","   -w /runtime \\","   -e ROOTFS_DIR=/crossrootfs/arm64 \\","-  mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net11.0-cross-freebsd-14-arm64 \\","+  mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet-buildtools/prereqs:azurelinux-4.0-net12.0-cross-freebsd-14-arm64 \\","   bash"," ```"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/workflow/using-docker.md","lines":["@@ -26,28 +26,28 @@ The main Docker images are the most commonly used ones, and the ones you will pr"," "," | Host OS           | Target OS    | Target Arch     | Image                                                                                  |